  "answer":"After a significant drift is detected, the handbook requires that a challenger model be trained and evaluated, with a control batch evaluated before any alerts are trusted. Promotion of a new model is only permitted when the challenger meets the release criteria: it must improve F1 by at least 0.005 and its ROC‑AUC may not drop by more than 0.01 on a frozen holdout evaluation, and the release approver (the project owner) must approve the change. A drift alert by itself never authorizes promotion.",
  "sources":[
    {
      "source_id":"drift-runbook",
      "quote":"Drift triggers challenger training and evaluation, not immediate promotion. A control batch is evaluated before trusting alerts."
    },
    {
      "source_id":"release-policy",
      "quote":"Promote only when F1 improves by at least 0.005 and ROC-AUC drops by no more than 0.01. A drift alert alone never authorizes promotion."
    }
  ]
}
